entioned businesses may fail to deliver or default on agreements. Ultimately, business is about weighing risk versus reward. If your previous experiences and the experiences of your network suggest that the risk of financial loss is too high, and if the cost of mitigating those risks (through escrow, legal counsel, and third-party inspectors) erases your profit margin, the most prudent business decision may simply be to look for partners in a different, more stable market.
